module avin

// A value a Sysl binding's shim converts to one Sysl type and back. The compiler decides it for every
// type from the type's structure, so it is written only as a bound: a generic binding's type
// parameters, and a generic Sysl handle's, are bounded by it, `[T: Boundary]`, and so is every type
// parameter a generic function passes on to one.
//
// Boundary are the integers of 8, 16, 32 and 64 bits, `byte`, `real`, `char`, `bool`, `unit`,
// `string`, the data types declared with `@sysl` to mirror a Sysl enum or struct, and `Option`s,
// `Result`s and tuples of these. A collection, which crosses as a copy whose Sysl type differs by
// direction, a Sysl handle, which goes into Sysl only by itself, and every other class, data type and
// function are not.
trait Boundary
